window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/owner-courses/b211-408c3233273296fb.json"]={sha256:"408c3233273296fb54e6422a8656e7bff8d0b7eef54247417ff56c13a9d79096",value:{"id":"b211","title":"塔貝拉水壩","titleEn":"Tarbela Dam","category":"water","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"本課以以塔貝拉深厚地基防滲及既有水路擴建界面學習為主線，先用大體積填築物流與鋪蓋延伸與流路界定水力與構造條件，再將蓄水分期與孔壓、進水口餘隙與淤積連結到出口消能與修復證據。合成土石壩與水路模型不重現塔貝拉現況，實際地層、設備與調度須以業主資料另行建立。 每單元以原創算例、量測與失效辨識共同檢查推論。","summaryEn":"This course develops studying Tarbela foundation seepage control and existing-waterway expansion interfaces through Bulk placement logistics and Blanket extension and seepage paths, then connects Impoundment stages and pore pressure and Intake clearance and deposition to Outlet dissipation and repair evidence. Synthetic embankment and waterway models do not reconstruct Tarbela conditions; owner data must establish actual geology equipment and operations. Each unit combines original calculation, measurement and failure diagnosis to test the inference.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"water-dams","subcategoryTitle":"世界水壩與水庫","subcategoryTitleEn":"World dams and reservoirs","learningTrack":"water","learningSubdiscipline":"water-dams","learningTags":["water","water-dams","water"],"architectureFamily":"water-dam","architectureNodes":[["大體積填築物流","Bulk placement logistics"],["分層導水與各向異性","Layered conductivity and anisotropy"],["蓄水分期與孔壓","Impoundment stages and pore pressure"],["進水口餘隙與淤積","Intake clearance and deposition"],["出口消能與修復證據","Outlet dissipation and repair evidence"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[0,3]],"diagram":{"type":"water-dam","labels":["大體積填築物流","分層導水與各向異性","蓄水分期與孔壓","進水口餘隙與淤積","出口消能與修復證據"],"labelsEn":["Bulk placement logistics","Layered conductivity and anisotropy","Impoundment stages and pore pressure","Intake clearance and deposition","Outlet dissipation and repair evidence"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"整合算例輸入全為教學假設，先檢查大體積填築物流：trucks=20; payload=18 m3; cyclesPerHour=2; productiveHours=8; looseVolume=20*18*2*8=5760 m3/day；再獨立檢查鋪蓋延伸與流路：k=0.0001 m/s; effectiveArea=2000 m2; headDifference=60 m; pathLength=400 m; Q=0.0001*2000*60/400=0.030 m3/s。敏感度：同滲透係數與面積下，示意水路長度由400增至600m，達西流量減至三分之二；鋪蓋延長的真實效果需二維或三維流網，不能用此比例直接估算實際壩基改善。 兩個結果須按各自量綱解釋，不能直接相加或當成完整設計。合成土石壩與水路模型不重現塔貝拉現況，實際地層、設備與調度須以業主資料另行建立。 將比較改接前後能量線與接頭壓力並核對實際構形作為獨立驗證，明確列出尚缺的現地輸入及其對結論的影響。","textEn":"Every input in this integrated example is a teaching assumption. First examine Bulk placement logistics: trucks=20; payload=18 m3; cyclesPerHour=2; productiveHours=8; looseVolume=20*18*2*8=5760 m3/day. Independently examine Blanket extension and seepage paths: k=0.0001 m/s; effectiveArea=2000 m2; headDifference=60 m; pathLength=400 m; Q=0.0001*2000*60/400=0.030 m3/s. Sensitivity: at fixed conductivity and area, increasing an illustrative seepage path from400 to600m reduces Darcy flow to two-thirds. Real blanket extension requires a two- or three-dimensional flow model rather than direct use of this ratio. Interpret each result in its own dimensions rather than adding them or treating them as a complete design. Synthetic embankment and waterway models do not reconstruct Tarbela conditions; owner data must establish actual geology equipment and operations. Use the following independent check: Compare energy lines and joint pressures before and after connection and verify geometry. Identify missing field inputs and state which conclusions depend on them.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":15,"enrichmentVersion":15,"stages":[{"id":"b211-v15-s1","title":"水文條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Hydrology, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「大體積填築物流」與「鋪蓋延伸與流路」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Bulk placement logistics\" and \"Blanket extension and seepage paths\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b211-v15-01","title":"大體積填築物流：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Bulk placement logistics: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「大體積填築物流」如何影響塔貝拉水壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Bulk placement logistics” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Tarbela Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"塔貝拉的土石壩型式提供大量填築物流的學習背景，車輛載量、循環時間與有效工時共同限制日產量。理想車隊算例假設供料與攤鋪不成瓶頸，實際還需檢查材料分區、道路干擾與品質驗收速度，不能只加車就宣稱產能增加。 驗證時應核對過磅循環時間與攤鋪驗收紀錄並分別列鬆方實方，並辨識以下失效情境：把鬆方直接當完成實方會高估填築進度。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「大體積填築物流」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Tarbela provides context for large embankment placement logistics. Truck payload, cycle time and productive hours limit output. An ideal fleet estimate assumes loading and spreading are unconstrained; material zoning, road interference and acceptance capacity can become bottlenecks, so adding vehicles alone does not guarantee more placement. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Reconcile haul cycles with placement acceptance and distinguish loose from compacted volume. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Counting loose volume as completed compacted volume overstates progress. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Bulk placement logistics” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：trucks=20; payload=18 m3; cyclesPerHour=2; productiveHours=8; looseVolume=20*18*2*8=5760 m3/day。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: trucks=20; payload=18 m3; cyclesPerHour=2; productiveHours=8; looseVolume=20*18*2*8=5760 m3/day.","failure":"常見誤解：「增加運輸車數就保證攤鋪完成量同比增加」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"More haul trucks guarantee a proportional increase in accepted placement\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「大體積填築物流」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Bulk placement logistics”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b211-v15-01-k1","title":"大體積填築物流","titleEn":"Bulk placement logistics","text":"塔貝拉的土石壩型式提供大量填築物流的學習背景，車輛載量、循環時間與有效工時共同限制日產量。理想車隊算例假設供料與攤鋪不成瓶頸，實際還需檢查材料分區、道路干擾與品質驗收速度，不能只加車就宣稱產能增加。","textEn":"Tarbela provides context for large embankment placement logistics. Truck payload, cycle time and productive hours limit output.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"]},{"id":"b211-v15-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：增加運輸車數就保證攤鋪完成量同比增加 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: More haul trucks guarantee a proportional increase in accepted placement Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「大體積填築物流」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Bulk placement logistics\" is correct?","options":["增加運輸車數就保證攤鋪完成量同比增加","塔貝拉的土石壩型式提供大量填築物流的學習背景，車輛載量、循環時間與有效工時共同限制日產量。","鋪蓋越長就可不必檢查局部破損與邊緣效應"],"optionsEn":["More haul trucks guarantee a proportional increase in accepted placement","Tarbela provides context for large embankment placement logistics.","A longer blanket removes the need to inspect defects and edge effects"],"answer":1,"explanation":"塔貝拉的土石壩型式提供大量填築物流的學習背景，車輛載量、循環時間與有效工時共同限制日產量。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Tarbela provides context for large embankment placement logistics. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b211-v15-02","title":"大體積填築物流：定量估算","titleEn":"Bulk placement logistics: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"],"prerequisiteIds":["b211-v15-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「大體積填築物流」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Bulk placement logistics” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：trucks=20; payload=18 m3; cyclesPerHour=2; productiveHours=8; looseVolume=20*18*2*8=5760 m3/day。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: trucks=20; payload=18 m3; cyclesPerHour=2; productiveHours=8; looseVolume=20*18*2*8=5760 m3/day. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對過磅循環時間與攤鋪驗收紀錄並分別列鬆方實方。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Reconcile haul cycles with placement acceptance and distinguish loose from compacted volume.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b211-v15-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：trucks=20; payload=18 m3; cyclesPerHour=2; productiveHours=8; looseVolume=20*18*2*8=5760 m3/day。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: trucks=20; payload=18 m3; cyclesPerHour=2; productiveHours=8; looseVolume=20*18*2*8=5760 m3/day. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"]},{"id":"b211-v15-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「大體積填築物流」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Bulk placement logistics\", which statement holds?","options":["低於理想浮起梯度就排除所有內部沖蝕","三角洲前緣前進距離本身就是淤積體積","原創教學假設：trucks=20; payload=18 m3; cyclesPerHour=2; productiveHours=8; looseVolume=20*18*2*8=5760 m3/day。"],"optionsEn":["A gradient below ideal heave excludes every internal-erosion mechanism","Delta-front advance distance itself equals deposited volume","Original teaching assumptions: trucks=20; payload=18 m3; cyclesPerHour=2; productiveHours=8; looseVolume=20*18*2*8=5760 m3/day."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：trucks=20; payload=18 m3; cyclesPerHour=2; productiveHours=8; looseVolume=20*18*2*8=5760 m3/day。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: trucks=20; payload=18 m3; cyclesPerHour=2; productiveHours=8; looseVolume=20*18*2*8=5760 m3/day. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b211-v15-03","title":"大體積填築物流：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Bulk placement logistics: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"],"prerequisiteIds":["b211-v15-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「大體積填築物流」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Bulk placement logistics” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對過磅循環時間與攤鋪驗收紀錄並分別列鬆方實方。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「把鬆方直接當完成實方會高估填築進度」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Reconcile haul cycles with placement acceptance and distinguish loose from compacted volume. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Counting loose volume as completed compacted volume overstates progress. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以核對過磅循環時間與攤鋪驗收紀錄並分別列鬆方實方作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對把鬆方直接當完成實方會高估填築進度，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Reconcile haul cycles with placement acceptance and distinguish loose from compacted volume. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Counting loose volume as completed compacted volume overstates progress. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：把鬆方直接當完成實方會高估填築進度。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Counting loose volume as completed compacted volume overstates progress. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b211-v15-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對過磅循環時間與攤鋪驗收紀錄並分別列鬆方實方。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「把鬆方直接當完成實方會高估填築進度」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Reconcile haul cycles with placement acceptance and distinguish loose from compacted volume. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Counting loose volume as completed compacted volume overstates progress. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"]},{"id":"b211-v15-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以核對過磅循環時間與攤鋪驗收紀錄並分別列鬆方實方作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對把鬆方直接當完成實方會高估填築進度，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Reconcile haul cycles with placement acceptance and distinguish loose from compacted volume. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Counting loose volume as completed compacted volume overstates progress. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「大體積填築物流」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Bulk placement logistics\"?","options":["核對過磅循環時間與攤鋪驗收紀錄並分別列鬆方實方。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","原有隧道直徑足夠就不必檢查改接水頭損失"],"optionsEn":["Reconcile haul cycles with placement acceptance and distinguish loose from compacted volume.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Adequate existing diameter removes the need to check conversion head losses"],"answer":0,"explanation":"核對過磅循環時間與攤鋪驗收紀錄並分別列鬆方實方。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Reconcile haul cycles with placement acceptance and distinguish loose from compacted volume. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b211-v15-04","title":"大體積填築物流：失效診斷","titleEn":"Bulk placement logistics: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"],"prerequisiteIds":["b211-v15-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「大體積填築物流」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Bulk placement logistics” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把鬆方直接當完成實方會高估填築進度。診斷時應採取以下查核：核對過磅循環時間與攤鋪驗收紀錄並分別列鬆方實方，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Counting loose volume as completed compacted volume overstates progress. Diagnose it by the following check: Reconcile haul cycles with placement acceptance and distinguish loose from compacted volume. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「增加運輸車數就保證攤鋪完成量同比增加」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"More haul trucks guarantee a proportional increase in accepted placement\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b211-v15-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把鬆方直接當完成實方會高估填築進度。診斷時應採取以下查核：核對過磅循環時間與攤鋪驗收紀錄並分別列鬆方實方，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Counting loose volume as completed compacted volume overstates progress. Diagnose it by the following check: Reconcile haul cycles with placement acceptance and distinguish loose from compacted volume. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"]},{"id":"b211-v15-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「大體積填築物流」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Bulk placement logistics\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","把鬆方直接當完成實方會高估填築進度。","鋪蓋越長就可不必檢查局部破損與邊緣效應"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Counting loose volume as completed compacted volume overstates progress.","A longer blanket removes the need to inspect defects and edge effects"],"answer":1,"explanation":"把鬆方直接當完成實方會高估填築進度。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Counting loose volume as completed compacted volume overstates progress. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b211-v15-05","title":"鋪蓋延伸與流路：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Blanket extension and seepage paths: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"],"prerequisiteIds":["b211-v15-04"],"objective":"說明「鋪蓋延伸與流路」如何影響塔貝拉水壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Blanket extension and seepage paths” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Tarbela Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"上游防滲鋪蓋可改變進入地基的水頭分布與流路長度，不能只看壩體核心而忽略深部地基。均質一維達西式只是方向性示意，鋪蓋邊緣、分層及局部穿透會產生二維效應；需以孔壓分布和分區流量檢驗。 驗證時應用鋪蓋前後及壩基孔壓剖面檢查實際水頭分配，並辨識以下失效情境：鋪蓋局部缺口可能形成短流路而削弱整體效果。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「鋪蓋延伸與流路」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"An upstream blanket changes foundation entry heads and seepage paths, making foundation control distinct from the core. A uniform one-dimensional Darcy calculation illustrates direction only. Blanket edges, layering and penetrations create two-dimensional effects that require piezometric and zoned-discharge validation. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Compare heads across the blanket and foundation to establish the actual distribution. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: A local blanket opening can create a short path that undermines overall performance. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Blanket extension and seepage paths” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：k=0.0001 m/s; effectiveArea=2000 m2; headDifference=60 m; pathLength=400 m; Q=0.0001*2000*60/400=0.030 m3/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: k=0.0001 m/s; effectiveArea=2000 m2; headDifference=60 m; pathLength=400 m; Q=0.0001*2000*60/400=0.030 m3/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「鋪蓋越長就可不必檢查局部破損與邊緣效應」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A longer blanket removes the need to inspect defects and edge effects\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「鋪蓋延伸與流路」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Blanket extension and seepage paths”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b211-v15-05-k1","title":"鋪蓋延伸與流路","titleEn":"Blanket extension and seepage paths","text":"上游防滲鋪蓋可改變進入地基的水頭分布與流路長度，不能只看壩體核心而忽略深部地基。均質一維達西式只是方向性示意，鋪蓋邊緣、分層及局部穿透會產生二維效應；需以孔壓分布和分區流量檢驗。","textEn":"An upstream blanket changes foundation entry heads and seepage paths, making foundation control distinct from the core. A uniform one-dimensional Darcy calculation illustrates direction only.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"]},{"id":"b211-v15-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：鋪蓋越長就可不必檢查局部破損與邊緣效應 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A longer blanket removes the need to inspect defects and edge effects Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「鋪蓋延伸與流路」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Blanket extension and seepage paths\" is correct?","options":["鋪蓋越長就可不必檢查局部破損與邊緣效應","分層地基的水平與垂直導水率必定相同","上游防滲鋪蓋可改變進入地基的水頭分布與流路長度，不能只看壩體核心而忽略深部地基。"],"optionsEn":["A longer blanket removes the need to inspect defects and edge effects","Layered foundations must have equal horizontal and vertical conductivity","An upstream blanket changes foundation entry heads and seepage paths, making foundation control distinct from the core."],"answer":2,"explanation":"上游防滲鋪蓋可改變進入地基的水頭分布與流路長度，不能只看壩體核心而忽略深部地基。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"An upstream blanket changes foundation entry heads and seepage paths, making foundation control distinct from the core. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b211-v15-06","title":"鋪蓋延伸與流路：定量估算","titleEn":"Blanket extension and seepage paths: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"],"prerequisiteIds":["b211-v15-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「鋪蓋延伸與流路」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Blanket extension and seepage paths” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：k=0.0001 m/s; effectiveArea=2000 m2; headDifference=60 m; pathLength=400 m; Q=0.0001*2000*60/400=0.030 m3/s。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: k=0.0001 m/s; effectiveArea=2000 m2; headDifference=60 m; pathLength=400 m; Q=0.0001*2000*60/400=0.030 m3/s. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用鋪蓋前後及壩基孔壓剖面檢查實際水頭分配。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare heads across the blanket and foundation to establish the actual distribution.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b211-v15-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：k=0.0001 m/s; effectiveArea=2000 m2; headDifference=60 m; pathLength=400 m; Q=0.0001*2000*60/400=0.030 m3/s。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: k=0.0001 m/s; effectiveArea=2000 m2; headDifference=60 m; pathLength=400 m; Q=0.0001*2000*60/400=0.030 m3/s. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"]},{"id":"b211-v15-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「鋪蓋延伸與流路」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Blanket extension and seepage paths\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：k=0.0001 m/s; effectiveArea=2000 m2; headDifference=60 m; pathLength=400 m; Q=0.0001*2000*60/400=0.030 m3/s。","淺層孔壓穩定就表示整個地基都已達平衡","平均庫底夠低就保證進水口前沒有淤堵"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: k=0.0001 m/s; effectiveArea=2000 m2; headDifference=60 m; pathLength=400 m; Q=0.0001*2000*60/400=0.030 m3/s.","Stable shallow pressure means the entire foundation is at equilibrium","A low mean reservoir bed guarantees no intake-local blockage"],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：k=0.0001 m/s; effectiveArea=2000 m2; headDifference=60 m; pathLength=400 m; Q=0.0001*2000*60/400=0.030 m3/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: k=0.0001 m/s; effectiveArea=2000 m2; headDifference=60 m; pathLength=400 m; Q=0.0001*2000*60/400=0.030 m3/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b211-v15-07","title":"鋪蓋延伸與流路：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Blanket extension and seepage paths: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"],"prerequisiteIds":["b211-v15-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「鋪蓋延伸與流路」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Blanket extension and seepage paths” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用鋪蓋前後及壩基孔壓剖面檢查實際水頭分配。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「鋪蓋局部缺口可能形成短流路而削弱整體效果」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare heads across the blanket and foundation to establish the actual distribution. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: A local blanket opening can create a short path that undermines overall performance. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以用鋪蓋前後及壩基孔壓剖面檢查實際水頭分配作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對鋪蓋局部缺口可能形成短流路而削弱整體效果，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Compare heads across the blanket and foundation to establish the actual distribution. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: A local blanket opening can create a short path that undermines overall performance. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：鋪蓋局部缺口可能形成短流路而削弱整體效果。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A local blanket opening can create a short path that undermines overall performance. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b211-v15-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用鋪蓋前後及壩基孔壓剖面檢查實際水頭分配。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「鋪蓋局部缺口可能形成短流路而削弱整體效果」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Compare heads across the blanket and foundation to establish the actual distribution. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: A local blanket opening can create a short path that undermines overall performance. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"]},{"id":"b211-v15-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以用鋪蓋前後及壩基孔壓剖面檢查實際水頭分配作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對鋪蓋局部缺口可能形成短流路而削弱整體效果，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Compare heads across the blanket and foundation to establish the actual distribution. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: A local blanket opening can create a short path that undermines overall performance. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「鋪蓋延伸與流路」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Blanket extension and seepage paths\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","用鋪蓋前後及壩基孔壓剖面檢查實際水頭分配。","裝置容量乘全年時數就是保證可售電量"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Compare heads across the blanket and foundation to establish the actual distribution.","Nameplate capacity times annual hours equals guaranteed saleable energy"],"answer":1,"explanation":"用鋪蓋前後及壩基孔壓剖面檢查實際水頭分配。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare heads across the blanket and foundation to establish the actual distribution. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b211-v15-08","title":"鋪蓋延伸與流路：失效診斷","titleEn":"Blanket extension and seepage paths: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"],"prerequisiteIds":["b211-v15-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「鋪蓋延伸與流路」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Blanket extension and seepage paths” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"鋪蓋局部缺口可能形成短流路而削弱整體效果。診斷時應採取以下查核：用鋪蓋前後及壩基孔壓剖面檢查實際水頭分配，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A local blanket opening can create a short path that undermines overall performance. Diagnose it by the following check: Compare heads across the blanket and foundation to establish the actual distribution. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「鋪蓋越長就可不必檢查局部破損與邊緣效應」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A longer blanket removes the need to inspect defects and edge effects\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b211-v15-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"鋪蓋局部缺口可能形成短流路而削弱整體效果。診斷時應採取以下查核：用鋪蓋前後及壩基孔壓剖面檢查實際水頭分配，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"A local blanket opening can create a short path that undermines overall performance. Diagnose it by the following check: Compare heads across the blanket and foundation to establish the actual distribution. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"]},{"id":"b211-v15-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「鋪蓋延伸與流路」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Blanket extension and seepage paths\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","分層地基的水平與垂直導水率必定相同","鋪蓋局部缺口可能形成短流路而削弱整體效果。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Layered foundations must have equal horizontal and vertical conductivity","A local blanket opening can create a short path that undermines overall performance."],"answer":2,"explanation":"鋪蓋局部缺口可能形成短流路而削弱整體效果。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A local blanket opening can create a short path that undermines overall performance. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b211-v15-s2","title":"水力機制、材料與定量模型","titleEn":"Hydraulics, materials and quantitative models","description":"本階段聚焦「分層導水與各向異性」與「出口梯度與有效重量」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Layered conductivity and anisotropy\" and \"Exit gradient and submerged weight\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b211-v15-09","title":"分層導水與各向異性：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Layered conductivity and anisotropy: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"],"prerequisiteIds":["b211-v15-08"],"objective":"說明「分層導水與各向異性」如何影響塔貝拉水壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Layered conductivity and anisotropy” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Tarbela Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"沖積地基中水平連續砂礫層與低滲夾層可使水平及垂直導水率不同，單一等向係數可能誤判孔壓。平行層等厚加權只適用層內流向，跨層方向需用阻力式；應以鑽探和試驗建立層序與連通性。 驗證時應比較不同方向的試驗與孔壓反應並繪製連續高滲層，並辨識以下失效情境：把水平平均導水率用於垂直流會扭曲滲流分布。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「分層導水與各向異性」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Continuous granular layers and low-permeability seams create directional conductivity. One isotropic value can misrepresent pressures. Thickness-weighted averaging applies to flow parallel to layers, whereas cross-layer flow uses resistance weighting. Boreholes and testing must establish both layer sequence and hydraulic connectivity. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Compare directional tests and pressure response and map connected high-permeability layers. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Using horizontal averaged conductivity for vertical flow distorts the seepage field. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Layered conductivity and anisotropy” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：Parallel flow through equal-thickness layers: k1=1e-3 m/s;k2=1e-5 m/s; horizontalK=(1e-3+1e-5)/2=0.000505 m/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: Parallel flow through equal-thickness layers: k1=1e-3 m/s;k2=1e-5 m/s; horizontalK=(1e-3+1e-5)/2=0.000505 m/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「分層地基的水平與垂直導水率必定相同」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Layered foundations must have equal horizontal and vertical conductivity\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「分層導水與各向異性」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Layered conductivity and anisotropy”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b211-v15-09-k1","title":"分層導水與各向異性","titleEn":"Layered conductivity and anisotropy","text":"沖積地基中水平連續砂礫層與低滲夾層可使水平及垂直導水率不同，單一等向係數可能誤判孔壓。平行層等厚加權只適用層內流向，跨層方向需用阻力式；應以鑽探和試驗建立層序與連通性。","textEn":"Continuous granular layers and low-permeability seams create directional conductivity. One isotropic value can misrepresent pressures.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"]},{"id":"b211-v15-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：分層地基的水平與垂直導水率必定相同 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Layered foundations must have equal horizontal and vertical conductivity Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「分層導水與各向異性」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Layered conductivity and anisotropy\" is correct?","options":["沖積地基中水平連續砂礫層與低滲夾層可使水平及垂直導水率不同，單一等向係數可能誤判孔壓。","分層地基的水平與垂直導水率必定相同","低於理想浮起梯度就排除所有內部沖蝕"],"optionsEn":["Continuous granular layers and low-permeability seams create directional conductivity.","Layered foundations must have equal horizontal and vertical conductivity","A gradient below ideal heave excludes every internal-erosion mechanism"],"answer":0,"explanation":"沖積地基中水平連續砂礫層與低滲夾層可使水平及垂直導水率不同，單一等向係數可能誤判孔壓。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Continuous granular layers and low-permeability seams create directional conductivity. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b211-v15-10","title":"分層導水與各向異性：定量估算","titleEn":"Layered conductivity and anisotropy: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"],"prerequisiteIds":["b211-v15-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「分層導水與各向異性」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Layered conductivity and anisotropy” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：Parallel flow through equal-thickness layers: k1=1e-3 m/s;k2=1e-5 m/s; horizontalK=(1e-3+1e-5)/2=0.000505 m/s。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: Parallel flow through equal-thickness layers: k1=1e-3 m/s;k2=1e-5 m/s; horizontalK=(1e-3+1e-5)/2=0.000505 m/s. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：比較不同方向的試驗與孔壓反應並繪製連續高滲層。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare directional tests and pressure response and map connected high-permeability layers.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b211-v15-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：Parallel flow through equal-thickness layers: k1=1e-3 m/s;k2=1e-5 m/s; horizontalK=(1e-3+1e-5)/2=0.000505 m/s。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Parallel flow through equal-thickness layers: k1=1e-3 m/s;k2=1e-5 m/s; horizontalK=(1e-3+1e-5)/2=0.000505 m/s. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"]},{"id":"b211-v15-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「分層導水與各向異性」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Layered conductivity and anisotropy\", which statement holds?","options":["三角洲前緣前進距離本身就是淤積體積","原創教學假設：Parallel flow through equal-thickness layers: k1=1e-3 m/s;k2=1e-5 m/s; horizontalK=(1e-3+1e-5)/2=0.000505 m/s。","原有隧道直徑足夠就不必檢查改接水頭損失"],"optionsEn":["Delta-front advance distance itself equals deposited volume","Original teaching assumptions: Parallel flow through equal-thickness layers: k1=1e-3 m/s;k2=1e-5 m/s; horizontalK=(1e-3+1e-5)/2=0.000505 m/s.","Adequate existing diameter removes the need to check conversion head losses"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：Parallel flow through equal-thickness layers: k1=1e-3 m/s;k2=1e-5 m/s; horizontalK=(1e-3+1e-5)/2=0.000505 m/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Parallel flow through equal-thickness layers: k1=1e-3 m/s;k2=1e-5 m/s; horizontalK=(1e-3+1e-5)/2=0.000505 m/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b211-v15-11","title":"分層導水與各向異性：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Layered conductivity and anisotropy: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"],"prerequisiteIds":["b211-v15-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「分層導水與各向異性」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Layered conductivity and anisotropy” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"比較不同方向的試驗與孔壓反應並繪製連續高滲層。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「把水平平均導水率用於垂直流會扭曲滲流分布」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare directional tests and pressure response and map connected high-permeability layers. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Using horizontal averaged conductivity for vertical flow distorts the seepage field. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以比較不同方向的試驗與孔壓反應並繪製連續高滲層作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對把水平平均導水率用於垂直流會扭曲滲流分布，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Compare directional tests and pressure response and map connected high-permeability layers. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Using horizontal averaged conductivity for vertical flow distorts the seepage field. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：把水平平均導水率用於垂直流會扭曲滲流分布。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using horizontal averaged conductivity for vertical flow distorts the seepage field. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b211-v15-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"比較不同方向的試驗與孔壓反應並繪製連續高滲層。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「把水平平均導水率用於垂直流會扭曲滲流分布」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Compare directional tests and pressure response and map connected high-permeability layers. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Using horizontal averaged conductivity for vertical flow distorts the seepage field. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"]},{"id":"b211-v15-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以比較不同方向的試驗與孔壓反應並繪製連續高滲層作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對把水平平均導水率用於垂直流會扭曲滲流分布，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Compare directional tests and pressure response and map connected high-permeability layers. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Using horizontal averaged conductivity for vertical flow distorts the seepage field. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「分層導水與各向異性」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Layered conductivity and anisotropy\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","修復後損傷較少就不必比較前後水力工況","比較不同方向的試驗與孔壓反應並繪製連續高滲層。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Less postrepair damage removes the need to compare hydraulic conditions","Compare directional tests and pressure response and map connected high-permeability layers."],"answer":2,"explanation":"比較不同方向的試驗與孔壓反應並繪製連續高滲層。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare directional tests and pressure response and map connected high-permeability layers. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b211-v15-12","title":"分層導水與各向異性：失效診斷","titleEn":"Layered conductivity and anisotropy: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"],"prerequisiteIds":["b211-v15-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「分層導水與各向異性」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Layered conductivity and anisotropy” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把水平平均導水率用於垂直流會扭曲滲流分布。診斷時應採取以下查核：比較不同方向的試驗與孔壓反應並繪製連續高滲層，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using horizontal averaged conductivity for vertical flow distorts the seepage field. Diagnose it by the following check: Compare directional tests and pressure response and map connected high-permeability layers. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「分層地基的水平與垂直導水率必定相同」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Layered foundations must have equal horizontal and vertical conductivity\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b211-v15-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把水平平均導水率用於垂直流會扭曲滲流分布。診斷時應採取以下查核：比較不同方向的試驗與孔壓反應並繪製連續高滲層，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Using horizontal averaged conductivity for vertical flow distorts the seepage field. Diagnose it by the following check: Compare directional tests and pressure response and map connected high-permeability layers. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"]},{"id":"b211-v15-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「分層導水與各向異性」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Layered conductivity and anisotropy\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["把水平平均導水率用於垂直流會扭曲滲流分布。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","低於理想浮起梯度就排除所有內部沖蝕"],"optionsEn":["Using horizontal averaged conductivity for vertical flow distorts the seepage field.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","A gradient below ideal heave excludes every internal-erosion mechanism"],"answer":0,"explanation":"把水平平均導水率用於垂直流會扭曲滲流分布。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using horizontal averaged conductivity for vertical flow distorts the seepage field. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b211-v15-13","title":"出口梯度與有效重量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Exit gradient and submerged weight: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"],"prerequisiteIds":["b211-v15-12"],"objective":"說明「出口梯度與有效重量」如何影響塔貝拉水壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Exit gradient and submerged weight” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Tarbela Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"向上滲流可能減少顆粒骨架有效重量，出口梯度需與土的水下重量和拘束比較。臨界梯度簡式用於均勻無黏性土的浮起尺度，不是所有內部沖蝕的起始門檻；局部集中流與反濾失效可能在其他條件下發生。 驗證時應以出口附近密集孔壓量測核對局部梯度並觀察顆粒流失，並辨識以下失效情境：用平均全壩梯度代替局部出口梯度會漏掉集中作用。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「出口梯度與有效重量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Upward seepage reduces effective skeleton weight. A critical-gradient expression describes heave of uniform cohesionless soil, not the threshold for every internal-erosion mechanism. Concentrated flow and failed retention can develop under other conditions, so check local gradients and filter function separately. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Measure local exit gradients with closely spaced piezometers and observe particle loss. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: An average whole-dam gradient can conceal concentrated exit effects. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Exit gradient and submerged weight” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：grainSpecificGravity=2.65; voidRatio=0.65; idealHeaveGradient=(2.65-1)/(1+0.65)=1.00 dimensionless。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: grainSpecificGravity=2.65; voidRatio=0.65; idealHeaveGradient=(2.65-1)/(1+0.65)=1.00 dimensionless.","failure":"常見誤解：「低於理想浮起梯度就排除所有內部沖蝕」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A gradient below ideal heave excludes every internal-erosion mechanism\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「出口梯度與有效重量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Exit gradient and submerged weight”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b211-v15-13-k1","title":"出口梯度與有效重量","titleEn":"Exit gradient and submerged weight","text":"向上滲流可能減少顆粒骨架有效重量，出口梯度需與土的水下重量和拘束比較。臨界梯度簡式用於均勻無黏性土的浮起尺度，不是所有內部沖蝕的起始門檻；局部集中流與反濾失效可能在其他條件下發生。","textEn":"Upward seepage reduces effective skeleton weight. A critical-gradient expression describes heave of uniform cohesionless soil, not the threshold for every internal-erosion mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"]},{"id":"b211-v15-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：低於理想浮起梯度就排除所有內部沖蝕 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A gradient below ideal heave excludes every internal-erosion mechanism Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「出口梯度與有效重量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Exit gradient and submerged weight\" is correct?","options":["低於理想浮起梯度就排除所有內部沖蝕","向上滲流可能減少顆粒骨架有效重量，出口梯度需與土的水下重量和拘束比較。","淺層孔壓穩定就表示整個地基都已達平衡"],"optionsEn":["A gradient below ideal heave excludes every internal-erosion mechanism","Upward seepage reduces effective skeleton weight.","Stable shallow pressure means the entire foundation is at equilibrium"],"answer":1,"explanation":"向上滲流可能減少顆粒骨架有效重量，出口梯度需與土的水下重量和拘束比較。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Upward seepage reduces effective skeleton weight. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b211-v15-14","title":"出口梯度與有效重量：定量估算","titleEn":"Exit gradient and submerged weight: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"],"prerequisiteIds":["b211-v15-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「出口梯度與有效重量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Exit gradient and submerged weight” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：grainSpecificGravity=2.65; voidRatio=0.65; idealHeaveGradient=(2.65-1)/(1+0.65)=1.00 dimensionless。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: grainSpecificGravity=2.65; voidRatio=0.65; idealHeaveGradient=(2.65-1)/(1+0.65)=1.00 dimensionless. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以出口附近密集孔壓量測核對局部梯度並觀察顆粒流失。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure local exit gradients with closely spaced piezometers and observe particle loss.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b211-v15-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：grainSpecificGravity=2.65; voidRatio=0.65; idealHeaveGradient=(2.65-1)/(1+0.65)=1.00 dimensionless。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: grainSpecificGravity=2.65; voidRatio=0.65; idealHeaveGradient=(2.65-1)/(1+0.65)=1.00 dimensionless. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"]},{"id":"b211-v15-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「出口梯度與有效重量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Exit gradient and submerged weight\", which statement holds?","options":["平均庫底夠低就保證進水口前沒有淤堵","裝置容量乘全年時數就是保證可售電量","原創教學假設：grainSpecificGravity=2.65; voidRatio=0.65; idealHeaveGradient=(2.65-1)/(1+0.65)=1.00 dimensionless。"],"optionsEn":["A low mean reservoir bed guarantees no intake-local blockage","Nameplate capacity times annual hours equals guaranteed saleable energy","Original teaching assumptions: grainSpecificGravity=2.65; voidRatio=0.65; idealHeaveGradient=(2.65-1)/(1+0.65)=1.00 dimensionless."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：grainSpecificGravity=2.65; voidRatio=0.65; idealHeaveGradient=(2.65-1)/(1+0.65)=1.00 dimensionless。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: grainSpecificGravity=2.65; voidRatio=0.65; idealHeaveGradient=(2.65-1)/(1+0.65)=1.00 dimensionless. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b211-v15-15","title":"出口梯度與有效重量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Exit gradient and submerged weight: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"],"prerequisiteIds":["b211-v15-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「出口梯度與有效重量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Exit gradient and submerged weight” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以出口附近密集孔壓量測核對局部梯度並觀察顆粒流失。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「用平均全壩梯度代替局部出口梯度會漏掉集中作用」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure local exit gradients with closely spaced piezometers and observe particle loss. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: An average whole-dam gradient can conceal concentrated exit effects. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以以出口附近密集孔壓量測核對局部梯度並觀察顆粒流失作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對用平均全壩梯度代替局部出口梯度會漏掉集中作用，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Measure local exit gradients with closely spaced piezometers and observe particle loss. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: An average whole-dam gradient can conceal concentrated exit effects. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：用平均全壩梯度代替局部出口梯度會漏掉集中作用。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: An average whole-dam gradient can conceal concentrated exit effects. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b211-v15-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以出口附近密集孔壓量測核對局部梯度並觀察顆粒流失。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「用平均全壩梯度代替局部出口梯度會漏掉集中作用」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Measure local exit gradients with closely spaced piezometers and observe particle loss. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: An average whole-dam gradient can conceal concentrated exit effects. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"]},{"id":"b211-v15-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以以出口附近密集孔壓量測核對局部梯度並觀察顆粒流失作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對用平均全壩梯度代替局部出口梯度會漏掉集中作用，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Measure local exit gradients with closely spaced piezometers and observe particle loss. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: An average whole-dam gradient can conceal concentrated exit effects. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「出口梯度與有效重量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Exit gradient and submerged weight\"?","options":["以出口附近密集孔壓量測核對局部梯度並觀察顆粒流失。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","增加運輸車數就保證攤鋪完成量同比增加"],"optionsEn":["Measure local exit gradients with closely spaced piezometers and observe particle loss.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","More haul trucks guarantee a proportional increase in accepted placement"],"answer":0,"explanation":"以出口附近密集孔壓量測核對局部梯度並觀察顆粒流失。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure local exit gradients with closely spaced piezometers and observe particle loss. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b211-v15-16","title":"出口梯度與有效重量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Exit gradient and submerged weight: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"],"prerequisiteIds":["b211-v15-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「出口梯度與有效重量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Exit gradient and submerged weight” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"用平均全壩梯度代替局部出口梯度會漏掉集中作用。診斷時應採取以下查核：以出口附近密集孔壓量測核對局部梯度並觀察顆粒流失，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"An average whole-dam gradient can conceal concentrated exit effects. Diagnose it by the following check: Measure local exit gradients with closely spaced piezometers and observe particle loss. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「低於理想浮起梯度就排除所有內部沖蝕」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A gradient below ideal heave excludes every internal-erosion mechanism\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b211-v15-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"用平均全壩梯度代替局部出口梯度會漏掉集中作用。診斷時應採取以下查核：以出口附近密集孔壓量測核對局部梯度並觀察顆粒流失，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"An average whole-dam gradient can conceal concentrated exit effects. Diagnose it by the following check: Measure local exit gradients with closely spaced piezometers and observe particle loss. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"]},{"id":"b211-v15-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「出口梯度與有效重量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Exit gradient and submerged weight\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","用平均全壩梯度代替局部出口梯度會漏掉集中作用。","淺層孔壓穩定就表示整個地基都已達平衡"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","An average whole-dam gradient can conceal concentrated exit effects.","Stable shallow pressure means the entire foundation is at equilibrium"],"answer":1,"explanation":"用平均全壩梯度代替局部出口梯度會漏掉集中作用。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"An average whole-dam gradient can conceal concentrated exit effects. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b211-v15-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「蓄水分期與孔壓」與「三角洲推進與測深」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Impoundment stages and pore pressure\" and \"Delta advance and bathymetry\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b211-v15-17","title":"蓄水分期與孔壓：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Impoundment stages and pore pressure: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"],"prerequisiteIds":["b211-v15-16"],"objective":"說明「蓄水分期與孔壓」如何影響塔貝拉水壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Impoundment stages and pore pressure” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Tarbela Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"分期蓄水使工程師能比較庫水位改變與地基孔壓及變形反應，觀察時間需符合材料和儀器的反應尺度。單一升水步的平均速率不代表可接受操作速度；應按核准程序及失效模式判讀，並辨識尚未達平衡的深層測點。 驗證時應對照分期水位與深淺孔壓的延遲及穩定趨勢，並辨識以下失效情境：只看淺層孔壓穩定會漏掉深層尚未消散的變化。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「蓄水分期與孔壓」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Staged impoundment enables comparison of stage changes with pressure and deformation responses. Observation periods must fit material and instrument response times. A mean rise rate is descriptive, not an authorized rate; interpret it through approved procedures and failure modes and identify deep points still out of equilibrium. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Compare staged levels with shallow and deep pressure lags and stabilization trends. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Stable shallow pressures can hide continuing deep pressure changes. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Impoundment stages and pore pressure” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：HypotheticalStageIncrease=4.5 m; observationInterval=9 days; meanRiseRate=4.5/9=0.50 m/day。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: HypotheticalStageIncrease=4.5 m; observationInterval=9 days; meanRiseRate=4.5/9=0.50 m/day.","failure":"常見誤解：「淺層孔壓穩定就表示整個地基都已達平衡」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Stable shallow pressure means the entire foundation is at equilibrium\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「蓄水分期與孔壓」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Impoundment stages and pore pressure”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b211-v15-17-k1","title":"蓄水分期與孔壓","titleEn":"Impoundment stages and pore pressure","text":"分期蓄水使工程師能比較庫水位改變與地基孔壓及變形反應，觀察時間需符合材料和儀器的反應尺度。單一升水步的平均速率不代表可接受操作速度；應按核准程序及失效模式判讀，並辨識尚未達平衡的深層測點。","textEn":"Staged impoundment enables comparison of stage changes with pressure and deformation responses. Observation periods must fit material and instrument response times.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"]},{"id":"b211-v15-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：淺層孔壓穩定就表示整個地基都已達平衡 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Stable shallow pressure means the entire foundation is at equilibrium Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「蓄水分期與孔壓」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Impoundment stages and pore pressure\" is correct?","options":["淺層孔壓穩定就表示整個地基都已達平衡","三角洲前緣前進距離本身就是淤積體積","分期蓄水使工程師能比較庫水位改變與地基孔壓及變形反應，觀察時間需符合材料和儀器的反應尺度。"],"optionsEn":["Stable shallow pressure means the entire foundation is at equilibrium","Delta-front advance distance itself equals deposited volume","Staged impoundment enables comparison of stage changes with pressure and deformation responses."],"answer":2,"explanation":"分期蓄水使工程師能比較庫水位改變與地基孔壓及變形反應，觀察時間需符合材料和儀器的反應尺度。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Staged impoundment enables comparison of stage changes with pressure and deformation responses. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b211-v15-18","title":"蓄水分期與孔壓：定量估算","titleEn":"Impoundment stages and pore pressure: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"],"prerequisiteIds":["b211-v15-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「蓄水分期與孔壓」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Impoundment stages and pore pressure” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：HypotheticalStageIncrease=4.5 m; observationInterval=9 days; meanRiseRate=4.5/9=0.50 m/day。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: HypotheticalStageIncrease=4.5 m; observationInterval=9 days; meanRiseRate=4.5/9=0.50 m/day. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：對照分期水位與深淺孔壓的延遲及穩定趨勢。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare staged levels with shallow and deep pressure lags and stabilization trends.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b211-v15-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：HypotheticalStageIncrease=4.5 m; observationInterval=9 days; meanRiseRate=4.5/9=0.50 m/day。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: HypotheticalStageIncrease=4.5 m; observationInterval=9 days; meanRiseRate=4.5/9=0.50 m/day. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"]},{"id":"b211-v15-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「蓄水分期與孔壓」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Impoundment stages and pore pressure\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：HypotheticalStageIncrease=4.5 m; observationInterval=9 days; meanRiseRate=4.5/9=0.50 m/day。","原有隧道直徑足夠就不必檢查改接水頭損失","修復後損傷較少就不必比較前後水力工況"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: HypotheticalStageIncrease=4.5 m; observationInterval=9 days; meanRiseRate=4.5/9=0.50 m/day.","Adequate existing diameter removes the need to check conversion head losses","Less postrepair damage removes the need to compare hydraulic conditions"],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：HypotheticalStageIncrease=4.5 m; observationInterval=9 days; meanRiseRate=4.5/9=0.50 m/day。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: HypotheticalStageIncrease=4.5 m; observationInterval=9 days; meanRiseRate=4.5/9=0.50 m/day. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b211-v15-19","title":"蓄水分期與孔壓：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Impoundment stages and pore pressure: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"],"prerequisiteIds":["b211-v15-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「蓄水分期與孔壓」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Impoundment stages and pore pressure” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"對照分期水位與深淺孔壓的延遲及穩定趨勢。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「只看淺層孔壓穩定會漏掉深層尚未消散的變化」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare staged levels with shallow and deep pressure lags and stabilization trends. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Stable shallow pressures can hide continuing deep pressure changes. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以對照分期水位與深淺孔壓的延遲及穩定趨勢作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對只看淺層孔壓穩定會漏掉深層尚未消散的變化，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Compare staged levels with shallow and deep pressure lags and stabilization trends. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Stable shallow pressures can hide continuing deep pressure changes. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：只看淺層孔壓穩定會漏掉深層尚未消散的變化。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Stable shallow pressures can hide continuing deep pressure changes. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b211-v15-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"對照分期水位與深淺孔壓的延遲及穩定趨勢。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「只看淺層孔壓穩定會漏掉深層尚未消散的變化」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Compare staged levels with shallow and deep pressure lags and stabilization trends. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Stable shallow pressures can hide continuing deep pressure changes. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"]},{"id":"b211-v15-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以對照分期水位與深淺孔壓的延遲及穩定趨勢作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對只看淺層孔壓穩定會漏掉深層尚未消散的變化，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Compare staged levels with shallow and deep pressure lags and stabilization trends. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Stable shallow pressures can hide continuing deep pressure changes. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「蓄水分期與孔壓」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Impoundment stages and pore pressure\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","對照分期水位與深淺孔壓的延遲及穩定趨勢。","鋪蓋越長就可不必檢查局部破損與邊緣效應"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Compare staged levels with shallow and deep pressure lags and stabilization trends.","A longer blanket removes the need to inspect defects and edge effects"],"answer":1,"explanation":"對照分期水位與深淺孔壓的延遲及穩定趨勢。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare staged levels with shallow and deep pressure lags and stabilization trends. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b211-v15-20","title":"蓄水分期與孔壓：失效診斷","titleEn":"Impoundment stages and pore pressure: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"],"prerequisiteIds":["b211-v15-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「蓄水分期與孔壓」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Impoundment stages and pore pressure” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只看淺層孔壓穩定會漏掉深層尚未消散的變化。診斷時應採取以下查核：對照分期水位與深淺孔壓的延遲及穩定趨勢，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Stable shallow pressures can hide continuing deep pressure changes. Diagnose it by the following check: Compare staged levels with shallow and deep pressure lags and stabilization trends. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「淺層孔壓穩定就表示整個地基都已達平衡」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Stable shallow pressure means the entire foundation is at equilibrium\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b211-v15-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只看淺層孔壓穩定會漏掉深層尚未消散的變化。診斷時應採取以下查核：對照分期水位與深淺孔壓的延遲及穩定趨勢，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Stable shallow pressures can hide continuing deep pressure changes. Diagnose it by the following check: Compare staged levels with shallow and deep pressure lags and stabilization trends. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"]},{"id":"b211-v15-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「蓄水分期與孔壓」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Impoundment stages and pore pressure\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","三角洲前緣前進距離本身就是淤積體積","只看淺層孔壓穩定會漏掉深層尚未消散的變化。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Delta-front advance distance itself equals deposited volume","Stable shallow pressures can hide continuing deep pressure changes."],"answer":2,"explanation":"只看淺層孔壓穩定會漏掉深層尚未消散的變化。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Stable shallow pressures can hide continuing deep pressure changes. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b211-v15-21","title":"三角洲推進與測深：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Delta advance and bathymetry: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"],"prerequisiteIds":["b211-v15-20"],"objective":"說明「三角洲推進與測深」如何影響塔貝拉水壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Delta advance and bathymetry” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Tarbela Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"水庫泥砂三角洲推進會改變有效庫容與進水口周邊地形，前緣位移不等於沉積體積。用平均剖面積乘推進距離僅作稜柱近似，沿寬變化和壓密需另處理；應把斷面追蹤、粒徑與輸砂帳連結。 驗證時應沿多條測線追蹤前緣及斷面變化並核對沉積乾密度，並辨識以下失效情境：用單一中心線推進代表全庫寬會誤估沉積體積。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「三角洲推進與測深」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Delta advance changes storage and intake surroundings, but front movement alone is not deposit volume. Mean cross-sectional area times advance is a prism approximation that omits lateral changes and consolidation. Link repeated sections, grain-size observations and sediment budgets before interpreting long-term progression. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Track front and section changes along several transects and check deposit dry density. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Using one centerline advance for the full width misestimates deposit volume. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Delta advance and bathymetry” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：MeanDepositionalCrossSection=2500 m2; frontAdvance=120 m; prismDepositVolume=2500*120=300000 m3。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: MeanDepositionalCrossSection=2500 m2; frontAdvance=120 m; prismDepositVolume=2500*120=300000 m3.","failure":"常見誤解：「三角洲前緣前進距離本身就是淤積體積」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Delta-front advance distance itself equals deposited volume\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「三角洲推進與測深」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Delta advance and bathymetry”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b211-v15-21-k1","title":"三角洲推進與測深","titleEn":"Delta advance and bathymetry","text":"水庫泥砂三角洲推進會改變有效庫容與進水口周邊地形，前緣位移不等於沉積體積。用平均剖面積乘推進距離僅作稜柱近似，沿寬變化和壓密需另處理；應把斷面追蹤、粒徑與輸砂帳連結。","textEn":"Delta advance changes storage and intake surroundings, but front movement alone is not deposit volume. Mean cross-sectional area times advance is a prism approximation that omits lateral changes and consolidation.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"]},{"id":"b211-v15-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：三角洲前緣前進距離本身就是淤積體積 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Delta-front advance distance itself equals deposited volume Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「三角洲推進與測深」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Delta advance and bathymetry\" is correct?","options":["水庫泥砂三角洲推進會改變有效庫容與進水口周邊地形，前緣位移不等於沉積體積。","三角洲前緣前進距離本身就是淤積體積","平均庫底夠低就保證進水口前沒有淤堵"],"optionsEn":["Delta advance changes storage and intake surroundings, but front movement alone is not deposit volume.","Delta-front advance distance itself equals deposited volume","A low mean reservoir bed guarantees no intake-local blockage"],"answer":0,"explanation":"水庫泥砂三角洲推進會改變有效庫容與進水口周邊地形，前緣位移不等於沉積體積。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Delta advance changes storage and intake surroundings, but front movement alone is not deposit volume. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b211-v15-22","title":"三角洲推進與測深：定量估算","titleEn":"Delta advance and bathymetry: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"],"prerequisiteIds":["b211-v15-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「三角洲推進與測深」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Delta advance and bathymetry” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：MeanDepositionalCrossSection=2500 m2; frontAdvance=120 m; prismDepositVolume=2500*120=300000 m3。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: MeanDepositionalCrossSection=2500 m2; frontAdvance=120 m; prismDepositVolume=2500*120=300000 m3. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：沿多條測線追蹤前緣及斷面變化並核對沉積乾密度。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Track front and section changes along several transects and check deposit dry density.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b211-v15-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：MeanDepositionalCrossSection=2500 m2; frontAdvance=120 m; prismDepositVolume=2500*120=300000 m3。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: MeanDepositionalCrossSection=2500 m2; frontAdvance=120 m; prismDepositVolume=2500*120=300000 m3. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"]},{"id":"b211-v15-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「三角洲推進與測深」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Delta advance and bathymetry\", which statement holds?","options":["裝置容量乘全年時數就是保證可售電量","原創教學假設：MeanDepositionalCrossSection=2500 m2; frontAdvance=120 m; prismDepositVolume=2500*120=300000 m3。","增加運輸車數就保證攤鋪完成量同比增加"],"optionsEn":["Nameplate capacity times annual hours equals guaranteed saleable energy","Original teaching assumptions: MeanDepositionalCrossSection=2500 m2; frontAdvance=120 m; prismDepositVolume=2500*120=300000 m3.","More haul trucks guarantee a proportional increase in accepted placement"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：MeanDepositionalCrossSection=2500 m2; frontAdvance=120 m; prismDepositVolume=2500*120=300000 m3。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: MeanDepositionalCrossSection=2500 m2; frontAdvance=120 m; prismDepositVolume=2500*120=300000 m3. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b211-v15-23","title":"三角洲推進與測深：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Delta advance and bathymetry: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"],"prerequisiteIds":["b211-v15-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「三角洲推進與測深」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Delta advance and bathymetry” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"沿多條測線追蹤前緣及斷面變化並核對沉積乾密度。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「用單一中心線推進代表全庫寬會誤估沉積體積」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Track front and section changes along several transects and check deposit dry density. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Using one centerline advance for the full width misestimates deposit volume. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以沿多條測線追蹤前緣及斷面變化並核對沉積乾密度作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對用單一中心線推進代表全庫寬會誤估沉積體積，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Track front and section changes along several transects and check deposit dry density. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Using one centerline advance for the full width misestimates deposit volume. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：用單一中心線推進代表全庫寬會誤估沉積體積。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using one centerline advance for the full width misestimates deposit volume. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b211-v15-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"沿多條測線追蹤前緣及斷面變化並核對沉積乾密度。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「用單一中心線推進代表全庫寬會誤估沉積體積」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Track front and section changes along several transects and check deposit dry density. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Using one centerline advance for the full width misestimates deposit volume. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"]},{"id":"b211-v15-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以沿多條測線追蹤前緣及斷面變化並核對沉積乾密度作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對用單一中心線推進代表全庫寬會誤估沉積體積，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Track front and section changes along several transects and check deposit dry density. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Using one centerline advance for the full width misestimates deposit volume. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「三角洲推進與測深」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Delta advance and bathymetry\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","分層地基的水平與垂直導水率必定相同","沿多條測線追蹤前緣及斷面變化並核對沉積乾密度。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Layered foundations must have equal horizontal and vertical conductivity","Track front and section changes along several transects and check deposit dry density."],"answer":2,"explanation":"沿多條測線追蹤前緣及斷面變化並核對沉積乾密度。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Track front and section changes along several transects and check deposit dry density. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b211-v15-24","title":"三角洲推進與測深：失效診斷","titleEn":"Delta advance and bathymetry: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"],"prerequisiteIds":["b211-v15-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「三角洲推進與測深」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Delta advance and bathymetry” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"用單一中心線推進代表全庫寬會誤估沉積體積。診斷時應採取以下查核：沿多條測線追蹤前緣及斷面變化並核對沉積乾密度，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using one centerline advance for the full width misestimates deposit volume. Diagnose it by the following check: Track front and section changes along several transects and check deposit dry density. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「三角洲前緣前進距離本身就是淤積體積」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Delta-front advance distance itself equals deposited volume\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b211-v15-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"用單一中心線推進代表全庫寬會誤估沉積體積。診斷時應採取以下查核：沿多條測線追蹤前緣及斷面變化並核對沉積乾密度，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Using one centerline advance for the full width misestimates deposit volume. Diagnose it by the following check: Track front and section changes along several transects and check deposit dry density. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"]},{"id":"b211-v15-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「三角洲推進與測深」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Delta advance and bathymetry\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["用單一中心線推進代表全庫寬會誤估沉積體積。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","平均庫底夠低就保證進水口前沒有淤堵"],"optionsEn":["Using one centerline advance for the full width misestimates deposit volume.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","A low mean reservoir bed guarantees no intake-local blockage"],"answer":0,"explanation":"用單一中心線推進代表全庫寬會誤估沉積體積。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using one centerline advance for the full width misestimates deposit volume. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b211-v15-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「進水口餘隙與淤積」與「既有隧道擴建損失」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Intake clearance and deposition\" and \"Existing tunnel conversion losses\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b211-v15-25","title":"進水口餘隙與淤積：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Intake clearance and deposition: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"],"prerequisiteIds":["b211-v15-24"],"objective":"說明「進水口餘隙與淤積」如何影響塔貝拉水壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Intake clearance and deposition” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Tarbela Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"既有進水口的底部餘隙會隨沉積與庫水位變化，幾何淨距不足可能提高吸砂與堵塞風險。標高差只提供空間盤點，不預測局部三維取水或再懸浮；需同時觀測底床地形、流速與取水濃度。 驗證時應重測進水口前底床並比較取水含砂與局部流速，並辨識以下失效情境：只量遠處平均庫底會漏掉進水口前局部淤丘。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「進水口餘隙與淤積」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Intake clearance changes with deposition and stage, potentially increasing sediment ingestion or blockage. An elevation difference describes geometry, not three-dimensional withdrawal or resuspension. Combine bed surveys, approach velocities and intake concentration to interpret whether the remaining space is hydraulically adequate. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Resurvey the intake bed and compare sediment ingestion with local velocity. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: A distant mean bed level misses a local mound in front of the intake. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Intake clearance and deposition” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：IntakeLowerLipElevation=300 m; localSedimentElevation=292 m; verticalClearance=300-292=8 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: IntakeLowerLipElevation=300 m; localSedimentElevation=292 m; verticalClearance=300-292=8 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「平均庫底夠低就保證進水口前沒有淤堵」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A low mean reservoir bed guarantees no intake-local blockage\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「進水口餘隙與淤積」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Intake clearance and deposition”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b211-v15-25-k1","title":"進水口餘隙與淤積","titleEn":"Intake clearance and deposition","text":"既有進水口的底部餘隙會隨沉積與庫水位變化，幾何淨距不足可能提高吸砂與堵塞風險。標高差只提供空間盤點，不預測局部三維取水或再懸浮；需同時觀測底床地形、流速與取水濃度。","textEn":"Intake clearance changes with deposition and stage, potentially increasing sediment ingestion or blockage. An elevation difference describes geometry, not three-dimensional withdrawal or resuspension.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"]},{"id":"b211-v15-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：平均庫底夠低就保證進水口前沒有淤堵 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A low mean reservoir bed guarantees no intake-local blockage Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「進水口餘隙與淤積」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Intake clearance and deposition\" is correct?","options":["平均庫底夠低就保證進水口前沒有淤堵","既有進水口的底部餘隙會隨沉積與庫水位變化，幾何淨距不足可能提高吸砂與堵塞風險。","原有隧道直徑足夠就不必檢查改接水頭損失"],"optionsEn":["A low mean reservoir bed guarantees no intake-local blockage","Intake clearance changes with deposition and stage, potentially increasing sediment ingestion or blockage.","Adequate existing diameter removes the need to check conversion head losses"],"answer":1,"explanation":"既有進水口的底部餘隙會隨沉積與庫水位變化，幾何淨距不足可能提高吸砂與堵塞風險。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Intake clearance changes with deposition and stage, potentially increasing sediment ingestion or blockage. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b211-v15-26","title":"進水口餘隙與淤積：定量估算","titleEn":"Intake clearance and deposition: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"],"prerequisiteIds":["b211-v15-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「進水口餘隙與淤積」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Intake clearance and deposition” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：IntakeLowerLipElevation=300 m; localSedimentElevation=292 m; verticalClearance=300-292=8 m。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: IntakeLowerLipElevation=300 m; localSedimentElevation=292 m; verticalClearance=300-292=8 m. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：重測進水口前底床並比較取水含砂與局部流速。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Resurvey the intake bed and compare sediment ingestion with local velocity.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b211-v15-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：IntakeLowerLipElevation=300 m; localSedimentElevation=292 m; verticalClearance=300-292=8 m。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: IntakeLowerLipElevation=300 m; localSedimentElevation=292 m; verticalClearance=300-292=8 m. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"]},{"id":"b211-v15-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「進水口餘隙與淤積」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Intake clearance and deposition\", which statement holds?","options":["修復後損傷較少就不必比較前後水力工況","鋪蓋越長就可不必檢查局部破損與邊緣效應","原創教學假設：IntakeLowerLipElevation=300 m; localSedimentElevation=292 m; verticalClearance=300-292=8 m。"],"optionsEn":["Less postrepair damage removes the need to compare hydraulic conditions","A longer blanket removes the need to inspect defects and edge effects","Original teaching assumptions: IntakeLowerLipElevation=300 m; localSedimentElevation=292 m; verticalClearance=300-292=8 m."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：IntakeLowerLipElevation=300 m; localSedimentElevation=292 m; verticalClearance=300-292=8 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: IntakeLowerLipElevation=300 m; localSedimentElevation=292 m; verticalClearance=300-292=8 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b211-v15-27","title":"進水口餘隙與淤積：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Intake clearance and deposition: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"],"prerequisiteIds":["b211-v15-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「進水口餘隙與淤積」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Intake clearance and deposition” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"重測進水口前底床並比較取水含砂與局部流速。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「只量遠處平均庫底會漏掉進水口前局部淤丘」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Resurvey the intake bed and compare sediment ingestion with local velocity. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: A distant mean bed level misses a local mound in front of the intake. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以重測進水口前底床並比較取水含砂與局部流速作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對只量遠處平均庫底會漏掉進水口前局部淤丘，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Resurvey the intake bed and compare sediment ingestion with local velocity. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: A distant mean bed level misses a local mound in front of the intake. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：只量遠處平均庫底會漏掉進水口前局部淤丘。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A distant mean bed level misses a local mound in front of the intake. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b211-v15-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"重測進水口前底床並比較取水含砂與局部流速。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「只量遠處平均庫底會漏掉進水口前局部淤丘」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Resurvey the intake bed and compare sediment ingestion with local velocity. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: A distant mean bed level misses a local mound in front of the intake. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"]},{"id":"b211-v15-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以重測進水口前底床並比較取水含砂與局部流速作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對只量遠處平均庫底會漏掉進水口前局部淤丘，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Resurvey the intake bed and compare sediment ingestion with local velocity. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: A distant mean bed level misses a local mound in front of the intake. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「進水口餘隙與淤積」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Intake clearance and deposition\"?","options":["重測進水口前底床並比較取水含砂與局部流速。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","低於理想浮起梯度就排除所有內部沖蝕"],"optionsEn":["Resurvey the intake bed and compare sediment ingestion with local velocity.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","A gradient below ideal heave excludes every internal-erosion mechanism"],"answer":0,"explanation":"重測進水口前底床並比較取水含砂與局部流速。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Resurvey the intake bed and compare sediment ingestion with local velocity. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b211-v15-28","title":"進水口餘隙與淤積：失效診斷","titleEn":"Intake clearance and deposition: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"],"prerequisiteIds":["b211-v15-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「進水口餘隙與淤積」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Intake clearance and deposition” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只量遠處平均庫底會漏掉進水口前局部淤丘。診斷時應採取以下查核：重測進水口前底床並比較取水含砂與局部流速，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A distant mean bed level misses a local mound in front of the intake. Diagnose it by the following check: Resurvey the intake bed and compare sediment ingestion with local velocity. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「平均庫底夠低就保證進水口前沒有淤堵」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A low mean reservoir bed guarantees no intake-local blockage\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b211-v15-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只量遠處平均庫底會漏掉進水口前局部淤丘。診斷時應採取以下查核：重測進水口前底床並比較取水含砂與局部流速，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"A distant mean bed level misses a local mound in front of the intake. Diagnose it by the following check: Resurvey the intake bed and compare sediment ingestion with local velocity. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"]},{"id":"b211-v15-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「進水口餘隙與淤積」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Intake clearance and deposition\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","只量遠處平均庫底會漏掉進水口前局部淤丘。","原有隧道直徑足夠就不必檢查改接水頭損失"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","A distant mean bed level misses a local mound in front of the intake.","Adequate existing diameter removes the need to check conversion head losses"],"answer":1,"explanation":"只量遠處平均庫底會漏掉進水口前局部淤丘。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A distant mean bed level misses a local mound in front of the intake. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b211-v15-29","title":"既有隧道擴建損失：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Existing tunnel conversion losses: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"],"prerequisiteIds":["b211-v15-28"],"objective":"說明「既有隧道擴建損失」如何影響塔貝拉水壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Existing tunnel conversion losses” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Tarbela Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"把既有放水隧道接入新增機組時，流量與壓力邊界改變會影響摩阻和暫態，不能只查隧道直徑是否足夠。局部損失係數乘速度水頭可盤點轉接件作用，還需核對接頭、分岔與下游調節對整體系統的影響。 驗證時應比較改接前後能量線與接頭壓力並核對實際構形，並辨識以下失效情境：新增轉接損失會降低機組可用淨水頭。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「既有隧道擴建損失」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Connecting new generation to an existing release tunnel changes flow and pressure boundaries, affecting friction and transients. Diameter alone is insufficient. A local-loss calculation accounts for one transition, while joints, branching and downstream regulation require a system assessment under the converted operating conditions. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Compare energy lines and joint pressures before and after connection and verify geometry. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Added connection losses reduce net head available to the generating unit. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Existing tunnel conversion losses” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：AssumedTransitionK=0.35; meanV=9 m/s; localHeadLoss=0.35*9**2/(2*9.81)=1.44495 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: AssumedTransitionK=0.35; meanV=9 m/s; localHeadLoss=0.35*9**2/(2*9.81)=1.44495 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「原有隧道直徑足夠就不必檢查改接水頭損失」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Adequate existing diameter removes the need to check conversion head losses\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「既有隧道擴建損失」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Existing tunnel conversion losses”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b211-v15-29-k1","title":"既有隧道擴建損失","titleEn":"Existing tunnel conversion losses","text":"把既有放水隧道接入新增機組時，流量與壓力邊界改變會影響摩阻和暫態，不能只查隧道直徑是否足夠。局部損失係數乘速度水頭可盤點轉接件作用，還需核對接頭、分岔與下游調節對整體系統的影響。","textEn":"Connecting new generation to an existing release tunnel changes flow and pressure boundaries, affecting friction and transients. Diameter alone is insufficient.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"]},{"id":"b211-v15-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：原有隧道直徑足夠就不必檢查改接水頭損失 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Adequate existing diameter removes the need to check conversion head losses Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「既有隧道擴建損失」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Existing tunnel conversion losses\" is correct?","options":["原有隧道直徑足夠就不必檢查改接水頭損失","裝置容量乘全年時數就是保證可售電量","把既有放水隧道接入新增機組時，流量與壓力邊界改變會影響摩阻和暫態，不能只查隧道直徑是否足夠。"],"optionsEn":["Adequate existing diameter removes the need to check conversion head losses","Nameplate capacity times annual hours equals guaranteed saleable energy","Connecting new generation to an existing release tunnel changes flow and pressure boundaries, affecting friction and transients."],"answer":2,"explanation":"把既有放水隧道接入新增機組時，流量與壓力邊界改變會影響摩阻和暫態，不能只查隧道直徑是否足夠。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Connecting new generation to an existing release tunnel changes flow and pressure boundaries, affecting friction and transients. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b211-v15-30","title":"既有隧道擴建損失：定量估算","titleEn":"Existing tunnel conversion losses: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"],"prerequisiteIds":["b211-v15-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「既有隧道擴建損失」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Existing tunnel conversion losses” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：AssumedTransitionK=0.35; meanV=9 m/s; localHeadLoss=0.35*9**2/(2*9.81)=1.44495 m。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: AssumedTransitionK=0.35; meanV=9 m/s; localHeadLoss=0.35*9**2/(2*9.81)=1.44495 m. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：比較改接前後能量線與接頭壓力並核對實際構形。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare energy lines and joint pressures before and after connection and verify geometry.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b211-v15-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：AssumedTransitionK=0.35; meanV=9 m/s; localHeadLoss=0.35*9**2/(2*9.81)=1.44495 m。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: AssumedTransitionK=0.35; meanV=9 m/s; localHeadLoss=0.35*9**2/(2*9.81)=1.44495 m. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"]},{"id":"b211-v15-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「既有隧道擴建損失」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Existing tunnel conversion losses\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：AssumedTransitionK=0.35; meanV=9 m/s; localHeadLoss=0.35*9**2/(2*9.81)=1.44495 m。","增加運輸車數就保證攤鋪完成量同比增加","分層地基的水平與垂直導水率必定相同"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: AssumedTransitionK=0.35; meanV=9 m/s; localHeadLoss=0.35*9**2/(2*9.81)=1.44495 m.","More haul trucks guarantee a proportional increase in accepted placement","Layered foundations must have equal horizontal and vertical conductivity"],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：AssumedTransitionK=0.35; meanV=9 m/s; localHeadLoss=0.35*9**2/(2*9.81)=1.44495 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: AssumedTransitionK=0.35; meanV=9 m/s; localHeadLoss=0.35*9**2/(2*9.81)=1.44495 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b211-v15-31","title":"既有隧道擴建損失：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Existing tunnel conversion losses: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"],"prerequisiteIds":["b211-v15-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「既有隧道擴建損失」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Existing tunnel conversion losses” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"比較改接前後能量線與接頭壓力並核對實際構形。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「新增轉接損失會降低機組可用淨水頭」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare energy lines and joint pressures before and after connection and verify geometry. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Added connection losses reduce net head available to the generating unit. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以比較改接前後能量線與接頭壓力並核對實際構形作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對新增轉接損失會降低機組可用淨水頭，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Compare energy lines and joint pressures before and after connection and verify geometry. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Added connection losses reduce net head available to the generating unit. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：新增轉接損失會降低機組可用淨水頭。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Added connection losses reduce net head available to the generating unit. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b211-v15-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"比較改接前後能量線與接頭壓力並核對實際構形。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「新增轉接損失會降低機組可用淨水頭」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Compare energy lines and joint pressures before and after connection and verify geometry. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Added connection losses reduce net head available to the generating unit. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"]},{"id":"b211-v15-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以比較改接前後能量線與接頭壓力並核對實際構形作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對新增轉接損失會降低機組可用淨水頭，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Compare energy lines and joint pressures before and after connection and verify geometry. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Added connection losses reduce net head available to the generating unit. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「既有隧道擴建損失」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Existing tunnel conversion losses\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","比較改接前後能量線與接頭壓力並核對實際構形。","淺層孔壓穩定就表示整個地基都已達平衡"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Compare energy lines and joint pressures before and after connection and verify geometry.","Stable shallow pressure means the entire foundation is at equilibrium"],"answer":1,"explanation":"比較改接前後能量線與接頭壓力並核對實際構形。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare energy lines and joint pressures before and after connection and verify geometry. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b211-v15-32","title":"既有隧道擴建損失：失效診斷","titleEn":"Existing tunnel conversion losses: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"],"prerequisiteIds":["b211-v15-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「既有隧道擴建損失」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Existing tunnel conversion losses” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"新增轉接損失會降低機組可用淨水頭。診斷時應採取以下查核：比較改接前後能量線與接頭壓力並核對實際構形，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Added connection losses reduce net head available to the generating unit. Diagnose it by the following check: Compare energy lines and joint pressures before and after connection and verify geometry. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「原有隧道直徑足夠就不必檢查改接水頭損失」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Adequate existing diameter removes the need to check conversion head losses\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b211-v15-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"新增轉接損失會降低機組可用淨水頭。診斷時應採取以下查核：比較改接前後能量線與接頭壓力並核對實際構形，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Added connection losses reduce net head available to the generating unit. Diagnose it by the following check: Compare energy lines and joint pressures before and after connection and verify geometry. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"]},{"id":"b211-v15-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「既有隧道擴建損失」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Existing tunnel conversion losses\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","裝置容量乘全年時數就是保證可售電量","新增轉接損失會降低機組可用淨水頭。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Nameplate capacity times annual hours equals guaranteed saleable energy","Added connection losses reduce net head available to the generating unit."],"answer":2,"explanation":"新增轉接損失會降低機組可用淨水頭。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Added connection losses reduce net head available to the generating unit. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b211-v15-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「發電用水與放流協調」與「出口消能與修復證據」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Generation flow and release coordination\" and \"Outlet dissipation and repair evidence\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b211-v15-33","title":"發電用水與放流協調：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Generation flow and release coordination: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"],"prerequisiteIds":["b211-v15-32"],"objective":"說明「發電用水與放流協調」如何影響塔貝拉水壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Generation flow and release coordination” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Tarbela Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"新增發電功能可能利用原有放流水量，但發電時段與灌溉或下游需求的時間尺度不同。能量算例需清楚定義有效出力與時數，不能把裝置容量全年相乘當保證發電；水量與尾水限制需在共同調度邊界核對。 驗證時應以機組電量表與同期放流水量核對發電時窗，並辨識以下失效情境：把停機或缺水時段也當滿載會高估年度電量。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「發電用水與放流協調」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"New generation may use existing releases, but its timing can differ from irrigation or downstream needs. Energy requires defined output and duration; nameplate power times a full year is not guaranteed generation. Reconcile water and tailwater constraints within a common scheduling boundary. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Compare metered energy with release volumes over the same generating window. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Counting outages or water-limited periods as full output overstates annual energy. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Generation flow and release coordination” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：HypotheticalDeliveredPower=450 MW; actualGeneratingDuration=6 h; energy=450*6=2700 MWh。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: HypotheticalDeliveredPower=450 MW; actualGeneratingDuration=6 h; energy=450*6=2700 MWh.","failure":"常見誤解：「裝置容量乘全年時數就是保證可售電量」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Nameplate capacity times annual hours equals guaranteed saleable energy\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「發電用水與放流協調」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Generation flow and release coordination”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b211-v15-33-k1","title":"發電用水與放流協調","titleEn":"Generation flow and release coordination","text":"新增發電功能可能利用原有放流水量，但發電時段與灌溉或下游需求的時間尺度不同。能量算例需清楚定義有效出力與時數，不能把裝置容量全年相乘當保證發電；水量與尾水限制需在共同調度邊界核對。","textEn":"New generation may use existing releases, but its timing can differ from irrigation or downstream needs. Energy requires defined output and duration; nameplate power times a full year is not guaranteed generation.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"]},{"id":"b211-v15-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：裝置容量乘全年時數就是保證可售電量 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Nameplate capacity times annual hours equals guaranteed saleable energy Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「發電用水與放流協調」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Generation flow and release coordination\" is correct?","options":["新增發電功能可能利用原有放流水量，但發電時段與灌溉或下游需求的時間尺度不同。","裝置容量乘全年時數就是保證可售電量","修復後損傷較少就不必比較前後水力工況"],"optionsEn":["New generation may use existing releases, but its timing can differ from irrigation or downstream needs.","Nameplate capacity times annual hours equals guaranteed saleable energy","Less postrepair damage removes the need to compare hydraulic conditions"],"answer":0,"explanation":"新增發電功能可能利用原有放流水量，但發電時段與灌溉或下游需求的時間尺度不同。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"New generation may use existing releases, but its timing can differ from irrigation or downstream needs. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b211-v15-34","title":"發電用水與放流協調：定量估算","titleEn":"Generation flow and release coordination: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"],"prerequisiteIds":["b211-v15-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「發電用水與放流協調」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Generation flow and release coordination” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：HypotheticalDeliveredPower=450 MW; actualGeneratingDuration=6 h; energy=450*6=2700 MWh。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: HypotheticalDeliveredPower=450 MW; actualGeneratingDuration=6 h; energy=450*6=2700 MWh. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以機組電量表與同期放流水量核對發電時窗。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare metered energy with release volumes over the same generating window.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b211-v15-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：HypotheticalDeliveredPower=450 MW; actualGeneratingDuration=6 h; energy=450*6=2700 MWh。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: HypotheticalDeliveredPower=450 MW; actualGeneratingDuration=6 h; energy=450*6=2700 MWh. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"]},{"id":"b211-v15-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「發電用水與放流協調」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Generation flow and release coordination\", which statement holds?","options":["鋪蓋越長就可不必檢查局部破損與邊緣效應","原創教學假設：HypotheticalDeliveredPower=450 MW; actualGeneratingDuration=6 h; energy=450*6=2700 MWh。","低於理想浮起梯度就排除所有內部沖蝕"],"optionsEn":["A longer blanket removes the need to inspect defects and edge effects","Original teaching assumptions: HypotheticalDeliveredPower=450 MW; actualGeneratingDuration=6 h; energy=450*6=2700 MWh.","A gradient below ideal heave excludes every internal-erosion mechanism"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：HypotheticalDeliveredPower=450 MW; actualGeneratingDuration=6 h; energy=450*6=2700 MWh。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: HypotheticalDeliveredPower=450 MW; actualGeneratingDuration=6 h; energy=450*6=2700 MWh. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b211-v15-35","title":"發電用水與放流協調：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Generation flow and release coordination: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"],"prerequisiteIds":["b211-v15-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「發電用水與放流協調」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Generation flow and release coordination” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以機組電量表與同期放流水量核對發電時窗。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「把停機或缺水時段也當滿載會高估年度電量」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare metered energy with release volumes over the same generating window. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Counting outages or water-limited periods as full output overstates annual energy. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以以機組電量表與同期放流水量核對發電時窗作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對把停機或缺水時段也當滿載會高估年度電量，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Compare metered energy with release volumes over the same generating window. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Counting outages or water-limited periods as full output overstates annual energy. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：把停機或缺水時段也當滿載會高估年度電量。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Counting outages or water-limited periods as full output overstates annual energy. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b211-v15-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以機組電量表與同期放流水量核對發電時窗。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「把停機或缺水時段也當滿載會高估年度電量」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Compare metered energy with release volumes over the same generating window. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Counting outages or water-limited periods as full output overstates annual energy. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"]},{"id":"b211-v15-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以以機組電量表與同期放流水量核對發電時窗作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對把停機或缺水時段也當滿載會高估年度電量，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Compare metered energy with release volumes over the same generating window. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Counting outages or water-limited periods as full output overstates annual energy. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「發電用水與放流協調」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Generation flow and release coordination\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","三角洲前緣前進距離本身就是淤積體積","以機組電量表與同期放流水量核對發電時窗。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Delta-front advance distance itself equals deposited volume","Compare metered energy with release volumes over the same generating window."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以機組電量表與同期放流水量核對發電時窗。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare metered energy with release volumes over the same generating window. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b211-v15-36","title":"發電用水與放流協調：失效診斷","titleEn":"Generation flow and release coordination: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"],"prerequisiteIds":["b211-v15-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「發電用水與放流協調」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Generation flow and release coordination” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把停機或缺水時段也當滿載會高估年度電量。診斷時應採取以下查核：以機組電量表與同期放流水量核對發電時窗，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Counting outages or water-limited periods as full output overstates annual energy. Diagnose it by the following check: Compare metered energy with release volumes over the same generating window. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「裝置容量乘全年時數就是保證可售電量」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Nameplate capacity times annual hours equals guaranteed saleable energy\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b211-v15-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把停機或缺水時段也當滿載會高估年度電量。診斷時應採取以下查核：以機組電量表與同期放流水量核對發電時窗，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Counting outages or water-limited periods as full output overstates annual energy. Diagnose it by the following check: Compare metered energy with release volumes over the same generating window. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"]},{"id":"b211-v15-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「發電用水與放流協調」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Generation flow and release coordination\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["把停機或缺水時段也當滿載會高估年度電量。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","修復後損傷較少就不必比較前後水力工況"],"optionsEn":["Counting outages or water-limited periods as full output overstates annual energy.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Less postrepair damage removes the need to compare hydraulic conditions"],"answer":0,"explanation":"把停機或缺水時段也當滿載會高估年度電量。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Counting outages or water-limited periods as full output overstates annual energy. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b211-v15-37","title":"出口消能與修復證據：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Outlet dissipation and repair evidence: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"],"prerequisiteIds":["b211-v15-36"],"objective":"說明「出口消能與修復證據」如何影響塔貝拉水壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Outlet dissipation and repair evidence” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Tarbela Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"大型低位出口將高水頭轉為高速射流，下游消能與岩床反應必須和洞內壓力一起評估。水力功率給能量速率，不能直接預測沖坑深度；修復前後需以相同流量尾水比較壓力、地形及材料損傷，避免混淆工況改善與構造改善。 驗證時應對齊修復前後流量尾水並比較水墊壓力及沖坑測深，並辨識以下失效情境：較小洪水後損傷減少不一定證明修復構造更有效。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「出口消能與修復證據」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Large low outlets convert head into jets, requiring linked assessment of tunnel pressure, dissipation and the receiving bed. Hydraulic power is an energy rate rather than a scour-depth law. Compare repairs at matching discharge and tailwater using pressures, surveys and damage records to separate operating changes from structural improvement. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Match discharge and tailwater before and after repair and compare pool pressure and scour surveys. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Less damage after a smaller flood does not by itself prove a better repair. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Outlet dissipation and repair evidence” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：Q=150 m3/s; dissipatedHead=70 m; rho=1000 kg/m3; hydraulicPower=1000*9.81*150*70/1e6=103.005 MW。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: Q=150 m3/s; dissipatedHead=70 m; rho=1000 kg/m3; hydraulicPower=1000*9.81*150*70/1e6=103.005 MW.","failure":"常見誤解：「修復後損傷較少就不必比較前後水力工況」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Less postrepair damage removes the need to compare hydraulic conditions\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「出口消能與修復證據」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Outlet dissipation and repair evidence”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b211-v15-37-k1","title":"出口消能與修復證據","titleEn":"Outlet dissipation and repair evidence","text":"大型低位出口將高水頭轉為高速射流，下游消能與岩床反應必須和洞內壓力一起評估。水力功率給能量速率，不能直接預測沖坑深度；修復前後需以相同流量尾水比較壓力、地形及材料損傷，避免混淆工況改善與構造改善。","textEn":"Large low outlets convert head into jets, requiring linked assessment of tunnel pressure, dissipation and the receiving bed. Hydraulic power is an energy rate rather than a scour-depth law.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"]},{"id":"b211-v15-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：修復後損傷較少就不必比較前後水力工況 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Less postrepair damage removes the need to compare hydraulic conditions Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「出口消能與修復證據」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Outlet dissipation and repair evidence\" is correct?","options":["修復後損傷較少就不必比較前後水力工況","大型低位出口將高水頭轉為高速射流，下游消能與岩床反應必須和洞內壓力一起評估。","增加運輸車數就保證攤鋪完成量同比增加"],"optionsEn":["Less postrepair damage removes the need to compare hydraulic conditions","Large low outlets convert head into jets, requiring linked assessment of tunnel pressure, dissipation and the receiving bed.","More haul trucks guarantee a proportional increase in accepted placement"],"answer":1,"explanation":"大型低位出口將高水頭轉為高速射流，下游消能與岩床反應必須和洞內壓力一起評估。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Large low outlets convert head into jets, requiring linked assessment of tunnel pressure, dissipation and the receiving bed. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b211-v15-38","title":"出口消能與修復證據：定量估算","titleEn":"Outlet dissipation and repair evidence: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"],"prerequisiteIds":["b211-v15-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「出口消能與修復證據」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Outlet dissipation and repair evidence” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：Q=150 m3/s; dissipatedHead=70 m; rho=1000 kg/m3; hydraulicPower=1000*9.81*150*70/1e6=103.005 MW。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: Q=150 m3/s; dissipatedHead=70 m; rho=1000 kg/m3; hydraulicPower=1000*9.81*150*70/1e6=103.005 MW. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：對齊修復前後流量尾水並比較水墊壓力及沖坑測深。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Match discharge and tailwater before and after repair and compare pool pressure and scour surveys.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b211-v15-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：Q=150 m3/s; dissipatedHead=70 m; rho=1000 kg/m3; hydraulicPower=1000*9.81*150*70/1e6=103.005 MW。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Q=150 m3/s; dissipatedHead=70 m; rho=1000 kg/m3; hydraulicPower=1000*9.81*150*70/1e6=103.005 MW. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"]},{"id":"b211-v15-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「出口消能與修復證據」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Outlet dissipation and repair evidence\", which statement holds?","options":["分層地基的水平與垂直導水率必定相同","淺層孔壓穩定就表示整個地基都已達平衡","原創教學假設：Q=150 m3/s; dissipatedHead=70 m; rho=1000 kg/m3; hydraulicPower=1000*9.81*150*70/1e6=103.005 MW。"],"optionsEn":["Layered foundations must have equal horizontal and vertical conductivity","Stable shallow pressure means the entire foundation is at equilibrium","Original teaching assumptions: Q=150 m3/s; dissipatedHead=70 m; rho=1000 kg/m3; hydraulicPower=1000*9.81*150*70/1e6=103.005 MW."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：Q=150 m3/s; dissipatedHead=70 m; rho=1000 kg/m3; hydraulicPower=1000*9.81*150*70/1e6=103.005 MW。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Q=150 m3/s; dissipatedHead=70 m; rho=1000 kg/m3; hydraulicPower=1000*9.81*150*70/1e6=103.005 MW. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b211-v15-39","title":"出口消能與修復證據：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Outlet dissipation and repair evidence: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"],"prerequisiteIds":["b211-v15-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「出口消能與修復證據」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Outlet dissipation and repair evidence” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"對齊修復前後流量尾水並比較水墊壓力及沖坑測深。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「較小洪水後損傷減少不一定證明修復構造更有效」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Match discharge and tailwater before and after repair and compare pool pressure and scour surveys. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Less damage after a smaller flood does not by itself prove a better repair. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以對齊修復前後流量尾水並比較水墊壓力及沖坑測深作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對較小洪水後損傷減少不一定證明修復構造更有效，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Match discharge and tailwater before and after repair and compare pool pressure and scour surveys. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Less damage after a smaller flood does not by itself prove a better repair. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：較小洪水後損傷減少不一定證明修復構造更有效。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Less damage after a smaller flood does not by itself prove a better repair. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b211-v15-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"對齊修復前後流量尾水並比較水墊壓力及沖坑測深。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「較小洪水後損傷減少不一定證明修復構造更有效」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Match discharge and tailwater before and after repair and compare pool pressure and scour surveys. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Less damage after a smaller flood does not by itself prove a better repair. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"]},{"id":"b211-v15-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以對齊修復前後流量尾水並比較水墊壓力及沖坑測深作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對較小洪水後損傷減少不一定證明修復構造更有效，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Match discharge and tailwater before and after repair and compare pool pressure and scour surveys. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Less damage after a smaller flood does not by itself prove a better repair. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「出口消能與修復證據」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Outlet dissipation and repair evidence\"?","options":["對齊修復前後流量尾水並比較水墊壓力及沖坑測深。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","平均庫底夠低就保證進水口前沒有淤堵"],"optionsEn":["Match discharge and tailwater before and after repair and compare pool pressure and scour surveys.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","A low mean reservoir bed guarantees no intake-local blockage"],"answer":0,"explanation":"對齊修復前後流量尾水並比較水墊壓力及沖坑測深。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Match discharge and tailwater before and after repair and compare pool pressure and scour surveys. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b211-v15-40","title":"出口消能與修復證據：失效診斷","titleEn":"Outlet dissipation and repair evidence: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"],"prerequisiteIds":["b211-v15-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「出口消能與修復證據」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Outlet dissipation and repair evidence” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"較小洪水後損傷減少不一定證明修復構造更有效。診斷時應採取以下查核：對齊修復前後流量尾水並比較水墊壓力及沖坑測深，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Less damage after a smaller flood does not by itself prove a better repair. Diagnose it by the following check: Match discharge and tailwater before and after repair and compare pool pressure and scour surveys. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「修復後損傷較少就不必比較前後水力工況」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Less postrepair damage removes the need to compare hydraulic conditions\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b211-v15-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"較小洪水後損傷減少不一定證明修復構造更有效。診斷時應採取以下查核：對齊修復前後流量尾水並比較水墊壓力及沖坑測深，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Less damage after a smaller flood does not by itself prove a better repair. Diagnose it by the following check: Match discharge and tailwater before and after repair and compare pool pressure and scour surveys. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"]},{"id":"b211-v15-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「出口消能與修復證據」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Outlet dissipation and repair evidence\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","較小洪水後損傷減少不一定證明修復構造更有效。","增加運輸車數就保證攤鋪完成量同比增加"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Less damage after a smaller flood does not by itself prove a better repair.","More haul trucks guarantee a proportional increase in accepted placement"],"answer":1,"explanation":"較小洪水後損傷減少不一定證明修復構造更有效。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Less damage after a smaller flood does not by itself prove a better repair. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-wapda-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela","v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit","v15s-usbr-monitoring"],"curriculumVersion":15,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
